## Port of pumpkin/src/world/mod.rs
## PARTIAL: pumpkin/src/world/mod.rs - players, blocks and chunks: broadcasts, `tick`, `tick_environment`, `spawn_java_player`, `respawn_player`, `remove_player`, block get and set, `set_block_breaking`, `break_block`, `flush_block_updates`, active chunks, tick data. Missing, because what they call is a later batch: entities, block entities, block and fluid behaviour (`tick_chunks` computes the ticks and random ticks and has nobody to hand them to, `on_placed` and neighbour updates are the hook `blockHooks` below), sounds, particles, natural spawning, dragon fight, portals, explosions' block side, and the commands packet, an empty tree (src/command has no wire form yet). `drop_loot` needs item entities: a block's drops are not spawned. See ../block/block_place.aowl for `place_block`.
##
## The types are in ../serverbase.aowl.
##
## Upstream makes a joining client wait inside `spawn_java_player` until the chunk under it exists. Here one thread also
## answers every client, so that wait is a state, `Player.pendingSpawn`: `spawnJavaPlayer` sends what comes before the
## position and adds a ticket, and `continueSpawn` runs the rest when the chunk has arrived. A spawn chunk that does
## not arrive within `SpawnChunkPatienceMs` goes on without it, so a client is never left hanging: it gets its position
## and the chunk when there is one.

{.feature: "untyped".}
{.feature: "lenientnils".}

